The files of this directory are a modified version of the Haskell 98 Report,
"Haskell 98 Language and Libraries: The Revised Report", edited by Simon
Peyton Jones, in its online form of December 2002:
https://www.haskell.org/onlinereport/

They are not a definition of the language Haskell 98, and do not claim to be
one: they are part of an implementation of it, rhc.

What was changed:

  * Only the Haskell code of the Report's Prelude and libraries (chapters 8
    and 12 to 27) is here, not the Report in its entirety.
  * pristine/ holds that code as printed, taken mechanically from the HTML of
    the online Report (pristine/MANIFEST.tsv). It is kept unchanged, as the
    text the modules here are compared with.
  * The 20 modules here are that code with the published errata of the
    Revised Report applied, and the changes rhc makes to it, its overlay,
    and a comment at the head of each saying so. errata.tsv lists every
    erratum and what was done with it; the errata are
    https://www.haskell.org/definition/haskell98-revised-bugs.html
  * overlay.tsv lists every change made to the Report's code, or to be made
    to it, each with its reason.
  * PreludeEnum.hs holds 14 lines of the Report's Prelude, moved there.

PreludeBuiltin.hs and UnicodePrims.hs are rhc's own, not the Report's (the
modules of primitives the Report's code names and does not define), and are
under the CC0 1.0 Universal dedication of the rest of the Rune repository;
UnicodePrims.hs copies the tables of Rune's lib/unicode/code_point_data.sml.

The Report's notice, as the online Report gives it:

  Copyright (c) Simon Peyton Jones.

  The authors intend this Report to belong to the entire Haskell
  community, and so we grant permission to copy and distribute it for
  any purpose, provided that it is reproduced in its entirety,
  including this Notice. Modified versions of this Report may also be
  copied and distributed for any purpose, provided that the modified
  version is clearly presented as such, and that it does not claim to be
  a definition of the language Haskell 98.

The other files of this directory are distributed under that notice. The CC0
dedication of the rest of the Rune repository, in the LICENSE at its top, does
not apply to them.
